ring\n›\nFrom students and teachers\n“The clarity of your explanations, the way you demonstrate the concepts, and especially the quality of the questions you’ve developed are remarkable … I can absolutely see myself incorporating this into my classroom.”\nCameron C.\nTeacher, Roanoke, VA\n“I was very impressed with the quality of the physics visualizations … I will probably link to this site for my blog.”\nDoug N.\nProfessor, Rice University\n“I’m so glad I found this site because I’m taking physics right now and this is exactly what I needed to actually understand the concepts.”\nSerena O.\nStudent, University of Texas at Austin\n“I am using Atlas to essentially redo my college math and physics, as a refresher and brain stimulation. Awesome work!”\nMartin C.\nRetired electrical engineer\n“The clarity of your explanations, the way you demonstrate the concepts, and especially the quality of the questions you’ve developed are remarkable … I can absolutely see myself incorporating this into my classroom.”\nCameron C.\nTeacher, Roanoke, VA\n“I was very impressed with the quality of the physics visualizations … I will probably link to this site for my blog.”\nDoug N.\nProfessor, Rice University\n“I’m so glad I found this site because I’m taking physics right now and this is exactly what I needed to actually understand the concepts.”\nSerena O.\nStudent, University of Texas at Austin\n“I am using Atlas to essentially redo my college math and physics, as a refresher and brain stimulation. Awesome work!”\nMartin C.\nRetired electrical engineer\nAP Physics 1 and Physics C\nAP Calculus AB and BC\nAP Statistics\nNEW\nAP Biology\nNOV 3\nAP Chemistry\nNOV 5\nAP US History\nNOV 7\nAP Macroeconomics\nSOON\nAP US Government and Politics\nSOON\nAP Physics 1 and Physics C\nAP Calculus AB and BC\nAP Statistics\nNEW\nAP Biology\nNOV 3\nAP Chemistry\nNOV 5\nAP US History\nNOV 7\nAP Macroeconomics\nSOON\nAP US Government and Politics\nSOON\nAll subjects →\n1,163\nPRACTICE QUESTIONS\n177\nPRACTICE SETS\n34\nCHAPTERS · 3 SUBJECTS\nINTERACTIVE\nEvery figure turns, and comes apart.\n\nDrag to see it from any side. Tap a part to break it down, with its live numbers.\n\n↻ Drag to turn\nTap a part to break it down\nPRACTICE\nAP-style questions on every page.\n\nMultiple choice and numbers, graded as you go, in sets for each chapter. Any 3 sets are free with an account.\n\nPROJECTILE MOTION · SET 1 · 2 OF 4\n\nThe ball is thrown again with twice the sideways speed and the same upward speed. How far from the launcher does it land?\n\nA\nThe same distance\nB\nTwice as far\n✓\nC\nFour times as far\nD\n√2 times as far\nANSWERS ON THE FIGURE\nSee where your answer lands.\n\nEach question sets the figure to its own numbers. Get one wrong and your answer is drawn in, then the working plays out step by step.\n\nAI TUTOR PREMIUM\nStuck? Ask about that question.\n\nThe tutor sees the question, your answer and the working, so it can explain your mistake.\n\nStart with one lesson.\nCheck out a lesson →\nAtlas\nLearn\nSubjects\nPractice\nPlans\nPremium\nTeachers\nAtlas\nAbout\nsupport@atlasclass.app\nLegal\nTerms\nPrivacy\n© 2026 Atlas\nEnglish\nBahasa Indonesia\nBahasa Melayu\nTiếng Việt\n简体中文\n繁體中文\n日本語\n한국어\nहिन्दी\nEspañol\nPortuguês\nAP® is a trademark registered by the College Board, which is not affiliated with, and does not endorse, this site.",
